    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Two ways to say «two»",
     "texto": [
      "**两** is used before a measure word: **两 个 姐姐** («two older sisters»), **两 口 人** («two people in the family»). With 个, the number is usually **两**, not 二.",
      "**一些** means «some» and **每** means «each». **自己** is «oneself»; **家庭**, «family» as a unit."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
